@identity.sigil from Identity import { actor }
@slotted.sigil from Slotted import { app layer }
@rooms.sigil from Rooms import { room, room owner, room timezone, room lock }

component Availability {
  goal {
    Let a room owner say when a room is open, and tell other components the
    *open time* of a room over any range of dates.
  }

  interface {
    A room owner can add and remove a *weekly window*, a weekday with a start
    and end in room-local time on the *slot grid*.

    A room owner can add and remove a *blackout*, one whole room-local date on
    which the room is closed.

    Availability provides the open time of a room for a range of room-local
    dates, as spans of absolute instants.

    Availability provides each blackout of a room within a range of room-local
    dates.

    The *clock* is the single caller-supplied source of the current instant.
  }

  state {
    The slot grid divides room-local time into 30-minute slots.

    A weekly window starts and ends on the slot grid, may end at 24:00, and
    covers the half-open span from its start to its end.

    A weekly window must not overlap another weekly window on the same weekday.

    A *nonexistent local time* is a room-local time skipped by a daylight
    saving jump in the room timezone.

    A *repeated local time* is a room-local time that occurs twice because a
    daylight saving fall-back in the room timezone repeats it.
  }

  logic {
    Availability depends on Rooms for the room timezone and the room lock.

    Computing open time for a room takes a range of room-local dates from the
    caller and uses the room's weekly window list, its blackout list, and its
    room timezone from Rooms.

    For each room-local date in the range, it selects the weekly window list
    for that weekday.

    It then drops every date covered by a blackout.

    It then merges adjacent spans, including a weekly window ending at 24:00
    with one starting at 00:00 on the next date.

    It finally converts each span to instants in the room timezone, drops any
    slot at a nonexistent local time, and returns the open time.
  }

  constraints {
    Only the room owner may change a weekly window or a blackout.

    Availability must compute open time for each concrete room-local date and
    never precompute it as weekly spans in absolute time.

    A repeated local time resolves to its earlier occurrence.

    Every change to a weekly window or a blackout must run inside the room lock
    and must be invoked only by Booking, never directly by the app layer.

    Availability must not decline, cancel or flag any booking itself; it only
    reports open time.
  }

  decisions {
    Availability derives open time per date because daylight saving shifts move
    each weekly window relative to absolute time.

    Every change to a weekly window or a blackout goes through Booking because
    each change requires a sweep of pending requests on the room.
  }

  cases {
    A room is open Friday 18:00 to 24:00 and Saturday 00:00 to 02:00; open time
    is one continuous span from Friday 18:00 to Saturday 02:00.

    A weekly window from 01:00 to 04:00 on the spring-forward date in
    America/New_York gives two real hours of open time.

    A blackout on 24 December leaves no open time that date and does not change
    25 December.

    A weekly window at 09:00 to 12:00 in Asia/Kolkata aligns to the room-local
    slot grid although local 09:00 falls at half past the hour in UTC.

    An actor who is not the room owner tries to add a blackout; it is refused.
  }
}
